MOLY

A black root, a white flower.

The ground does not want to give it up. He pulls it out in front
of you anyway, without effort, the way you would take something
off a shelf.

He says the gods call it moly. Men have another name for it; he
does not say what that is. It is not a plant you have seen in
twenty years of walking about the world.

Carry it into the house. That is all it does. You do not eat it
or burn it or say anything over it. It sits in your hand, and
what is in her cup stops working.

    mv circe/.moly circe/house
